Previously, Beanstalk used constants in order to save gas costs. This limits composability and increases the friction of deploying contracts on L2 given the use of L1 addresses. This repo stores various Beanstalk Tokens (Bean, Unripe Bean, Unripe LP, Fertilizer) in state. A future area of improvement is to use the Diamond Storage standard in order to hardcode these addresses into bytecode, given that these values are set once upon deployment.

Additionally, various C.sol variables were removed due to them not being used anymore, or the ability to fetch them on chain with the 0.8.0 update (for example, block.chainId). 

